  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Regional Teacher Strategy for Latin America and the Caribbean</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Teachers are at the heart of quality education, yet many countries in Latin America and the Caribbean face challenges related to teacher shortages, professional development, working conditions and recognition of the teaching profession. This project supports the implementation of a regional strategy adopted by countries in the region to strengthen teacher policies and promote cooperation among governments and partners. The strategy was launched in August 2025 during a meeting of the Regional Committee for Education in the context of the World Summit on Teachers. Key activities include policy dialogue, technical assistance, knowledge sharing, capacity-building and the development of tools and evidence to support decision-making. Expected deliverables include regional meetings, policy guidance, analytical reports, training activities and cooperation initiatives that contribute to strengthening the teaching profession across the region.</narrative>
  </description>
